This is Fuzix for the DX-Designs P112
By Will Sowerbutts <will@sowerbutts.com>

Assumes a P112 fitted with 1024KB RAM and G-IDE

Supported hardware:
 - Real time clock (DS1302)
 - SMC floppy disk drive controller
 - G-IDE hard disk drive controller (IDE/ATA, register base 0x50)
 - Serial ports:
   tty1: ESCC channel A (RS232 levels on P4, standard boot ROM uses this port)
   tty2: ESCC channel B (TTL levels on P14 header; untested)
   tty3: ASCI channel 0 (TTL levels on P14 header; untested)
   tty4: ASCI channel 1 (TTL levels on P14 header; untested)
   tty5: SMC 16550A (RS232 levels on P8)

The serial ports require the use of RTS/CTS flow control.

This platform now builds with the fcc toolchain (asz80/ldz80). Build with:
    make TARGET=p112 all
in the "Kernel" directory. The result is "Kernel/fuzix.bin".

Disk: the root file system lives on the G-IDE disk (IDE/ATA). The SMC
37C665 floppy controller is supported as /dev/fd.

Boot (CF/IDE): "make diskimage" builds a bootable CF/IDE image. Sector 0
carries the P112 ROM (v5.8) G-IDE 0x2176 boot header; the ROM loads 32 sectors
to 0x8100 and runs tdboot, which relocates itself to 0xFC00, reads the packed
kernel from LBA 32 and enters it at 0x0088. The root filesystem is MBR
partition 0 at LBA 2048. It needs Images/p112/filesys.img (see
Standalone/filesystem-src).

Legacy boot paths (NOT TESTED since the fcc port): the CP/M loader
(fuzix.com, "make cpmimage") and the floppy boot sector (fuzix-boot.fdd,
"make floppyimage") are still in the tree but are still the original sdas
sources and have not been built or run with the fcc toolchain. Booting from
CP/M, the root filesystem device number can be given on the command line after
the command name, as a decimal number or a device name without the /dev
prefix (for example hda, hda1, hda2, fd0).
